  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at the Calvin Theatre in Northampton, Massachusetts, on Wednesday, November 8, 2017 [1]. This concert is the 242nd of 467 archived shows for the band, following a previous performance at the 9:30 Club on November 7, 2017 [2]. The recording, titled tMG2017-11-08, was taped by Bryce Carr and transferred by notasfarwest [1]. It is the only available recording of this specific date and features a 96-minute set with 21 songs [1]. The lineup includes tracks from albums such as Goths, We Shall All Be Healed, and The Sunset Tree [1]. Notable moments include the first archived performance of “Puffin’” and “New Chevrolet in Flames” [1]. “Poltergeist” is a bustout, appearing for the first time in 197 archived shows, while “Alpha in Tauris” is a rare track with only 11 archived performances [1]. The set concludes with four encores, including “Southwestern Territory” and “No Children” [1].",
